skill: "linkedin-growth"
sections[10]:
  - "\n"
  - "# linkedin-growth\n\nThe **LinkedIn personal-profile growth engine** — the profile as a landing page, what to post and how\noften, strategic commenting on target accounts, the golden hour, newsletters/video, and connections\nvs followers. The agent drafts posts + comment copy and designs the system; a human does the live\ncommenting/connecting; **scheduling-and-queue → WoopSocial** publishes the posts. Complements\n**linkedin-post-writer** (the single-post craft) and **linkedin-company-pages** (the page).\n\n"
  - "## The POV: dwell + comments, on a personal profile\nLinkedIn's algorithm rewards **dwell time** (people actually reading) and **early, meaningful\ncomments** — likes barely move distribution, and engagement bait is down-ranked. The feed is\nstructurally tilted to **people, not logos** (personal profiles get ~65% of feed allocation; pages\n~1–5%), external **links in the body suppress reach** (put them in the first comment), and posts now\nhave a **long shelf life** via suggested feeds — a good post travels for days or weeks. The cheapest\ngrowth lever isn't posting more: it's **thoughtful comments on bigger accounts in your niche**, which\nput your name in front of their audience daily. And in a feed where ~half the long posts are\nAI-written, **a specific, lived, first-person POV is the differentiator** — not volume.\n\n"
  - "## Read these first\n1. **brand-profile** — positioning, audience, non-negotiables.\n2. **voice-builder** — so posts and comments sound like one credible human.\n\n"
  - "## The framework: LADDER\n(Depth: `references/the-ladder-framework.md`.)\n- **L — Landing-page profile:** headline = value proposition (not job title); About opens with the\n  3 visible lines; Featured = the CTA; Follow-primary once inbound outpaces outbound. Every post's\n  job ends at a profile visit — the profile converts it. → **profile-optimization**.\n- **A — Author for dwell:** win the \"…see more\" tap, format for the read, mix text / document\n  carousel / native video / newsletter; **link in the first comment**. → **linkedin-post-writer**.\n- **D — Deploy strategic comments:** 5–10 substantive comments/day on target accounts in the niche —\n  the afterburner. A comment is content, not a courtesy. → **reply-and-comment-writer**.\n- **D — Drive the golden hour:** first 60–90 min decides reach; post in the audience window, reply\n  to every comment, comment around your own post time. Max **1 post/day**, 3–5/week.\n- **E — Expand with native surfaces:** newsletter (notification + email push), native video (the\n  2026 push), audio events; SSI as a directional health check, never the goal.\n- **R — Relationships & network hygiene:** connections (capped, ~100 invites/week) vs followers\n  (unlimited); no-pitch invites; DMs warm, not pitch-slaps. → **social-selling-and-dm**.\n\n"
  - "## The reality (verify-quarterly)\nFeed allocation and reach decline, dwell + comment weighting, the golden hour, link suppression,\nformat hierarchy (carousels/video/text), the see-more cutoff, creator mode's retirement, connection\ncaps, newsletters, SSI, the AI-content flood, cadence: `references/linkedin-2026-reality.md`. Post\ntypes + the commenting playbook + worked examples: `references/comment-and-post-recipes.md`.\n\n"
  - "## Honest scope (never violate)\n- **The engagement core is human** — the agent **drafts** posts, comment copy, invite notes, and DM\n  openers; a human **posts** the live comments, sends invites, and holds the conversations. No\n  auto-commenting, no auto-connect tooling (a restriction risk on LinkedIn specifically).\n- **WoopSocial schedules the posts** (text + media + optional link; native document carousels,\n  polls, newsletters, and audio events are posted/run natively). No update → delete + recreate. For\n  link-in-first-comment, the agent supplies post + comment; the pair is posted by tool/human.\n- **Post analytics:** impressions, reach, reactions, comments, and clicks come from **WoopSocial**\n  (LinkedIn Pages also reports engagement rate). **Profile viewers, followers, and SSI** stay on\n  **native LinkedIn**. **Never fabricate metrics.**\n- **No engagement bait, pods, mass-tagging, bought followers, or broetry theatre** — down-ranked by\n  the algorithm and quietly judged by the exact professionals you're trying to reach.\n  (Scope, distinctions + connections: `references/scope-and-connections.md`.)\n\n"
  - "## Distinct from its siblings (route correctly)\n**linkedin-growth (this)** = the PERSONAL-profile growth system (profile, cadence, commenting,\ngolden hour, features, network) · **linkedin-post-writer** = how to write one post well ·\n**linkedin-company-pages** = the page strategy + employee advocacy (advocates' personal posting\nroutes back here) · **reply-and-comment-writer** = drafting the comments/replies themselves ·\n**engagement-routine** = the recurring daily engagement block · **social-strategy** = the\ncross-platform plan.\n\n"
  - "## Where this connects\nReads first: **brand-profile**, **voice-builder**. Post craft: **linkedin-post-writer**,\n**hook-writer**, **carousel-writer** (document-carousel slides), **talking-head-and-piece-to-camera**\n(native video). Profile: **profile-optimization**. Engagement: **engagement-routine**,\n**reply-and-comment-writer**, **community-management**. Discovery: **social-seo** (headline/About\nkeywords), **ai-search-optimization** (LinkedIn is a B2B AI-answer source), **trend-jacking**.\nPipeline: **social-selling-and-dm**, **lead-magnets-and-funnels**; long-form owned channel:\n**email-and-newsletter**. Plan/measure: **social-strategy**, **goals-and-kpis**,\n**analytics-and-reporting** (native LinkedIn analytics). Publish: **scheduling-and-queue →\nWoopSocial** (posts; live comments/invites/DMs are human).\n\n"
  - "## Definition of done\nA profile audited as a landing page (headline = value prop, Featured = CTA, Follow-primary decision\nmade); a 3–5 posts/week plan, max 1/day, with links in the first comment and format mix mapped to\ndwell; a named list of 10–20 target accounts with a 5–10 comments/day playbook (drafted by the\nagent, posted by a human); a golden-hour routine (audience window, reply-to-every-comment); native\nsurfaces decided deliberately (newsletter yes/no, video cadence); connection-request hygiene with\nno-pitch invite copy; posts routed to scheduling-and-queue → WoopSocial with live engagement flagged\nhuman; metrics from native LinkedIn analytics + SSI directionally; no bait/pods/bought followers/\nbroetry; correctly distinguished from linkedin-post-writer and linkedin-company-pages.\n"
